{% doc %}
  Resolves a collection link to a URL that actually exists on the storefront.

  Demo content and theme-editor settings in this theme point at collection handles
  (gift-sets, lip-gloss, jewelry, ...) that a store may not have created yet.
  Emitting those handles straight into an href produces a hard 404, so any handle
  that doesn't resolve to a real collection degrades to the fallback instead.
  `/collections/all` is a virtual collection Shopify always serves, so it is safe
  as a default. Once the merchant creates the real collection, the original link
  starts resolving again on its own with no theme change.

  Non-collection URLs (pages, policies, external links) are passed through
  untouched — this snippet only validates /collections/ links.

  Outputs the URL. Capture it to use as an href.

  @param {object} [collection] - A collection object from a `collection`-type setting
  @param {string} [url] - A `url`-type setting value, e.g. "/collections/gift-sets"
  @param {string} [fallback] - URL used when nothing resolves. Defaults to /collections/all

  @example
  {% capture href %}
    {% render 'nani-collection-url', collection: block.settings.collection, url: block.settings.url %}
  {% endcapture %}
  <a href="{{ href | strip }}">Shop</a>
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign safe_fallback = fallback
  if safe_fallback == blank
    assign safe_fallback = routes.collections_url | append: '/all'
  endif

  assign resolved = ''

  comment
    A `collection`-type setting hands back a collection object. If it is populated
    the collection exists by definition, so its own .url is always safe.
  endcomment
  if collection != blank and collection.handle != blank
    assign resolved = collection.url

  elsif url != blank
    if url contains '/collections/'
      comment
        Covers both "/collections/<handle>" and "shopify://collections/<handle>",
        and tolerates a trailing query string or anchor.
      endcomment
      assign handle = url | split: '/collections/' | last | split: '?' | first | split: '#' | first | split: '/' | first

      comment
        Shopify normally resolves a `shopify://` setting to a real path before it
        reaches Liquid. If one ever slips through unresolved it would 404 as a
        relative href, so rebuild it from routes instead of echoing it back.
      endcomment
      assign safe_url = url
      if url contains 'shopify://'
        assign safe_url = routes.collections_url | append: '/' | append: handle
      endif

      if handle == 'all'
        assign resolved = safe_url
      elsif collections[handle].handle != blank
        assign resolved = safe_url
      endif
    else
      comment
        Not a collection link (page, policy, external) — leave it alone.
      endcomment
      assign resolved = url
    endif
  endif

  if resolved == blank
    assign resolved = safe_fallback
  endif
-%}
{{- resolved -}}
